69
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:07,010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the hardworking team of the Department of Tourism,

70
00:12:07,610 --> 00:12:15,310
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: good evening and welcome to the Department's budget briefing.

71
00:12:15,310 --> 00:12:21,430
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It is a privilege to preside over our deliberations on a sector that continues to generate jobs,

72
00:12:21,890 --> 00:12:25,250
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: sustain local enterprises, strengthen communities,

73
00:12:25,530 --> 00:12:28,770
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and showcase to the world why they should love the Philippines,

74
00:12:29,190 --> 00:12:34,930
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: while encouraging Filipinos and visitors alike to discover more to love across our country.

75
00:12:35,590 --> 00:12:37,530
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: This evening, we have the opportunity to hear from the Department of Tourism,

76
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:41,730
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and to hear from our newly appointed Tourism Secretary, Sec. Dita Angara Mathay,

77
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:46,150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: who has taken on the important responsibility of leading this vital sector.

78
00:12:46,650 --> 00:12:50,470
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: At the same time, it is our duty in Congress to constructively examine

79
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:55,250
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: whether the Department's proposed budget responds to the needs of Philippine tourism,

80
00:12:55,810 --> 00:12:59,630
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and whether every peso we invest translates into more visitors,

81
00:13:00,290 --> 00:13:03,210
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: better infrastructure, stronger tourism enterprises,

82
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:06,030
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and more opportunities for our people.

83
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:10,010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and the importance of this sector is clear from the numbers.

84
00:13:10,250 --> 00:13:16,330
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: In 2025, tourism generated 2.27 trillion in tourism direct gross value added,

85
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:23,390
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: equivalent to 8.1% of our GDP, while supporting millions of Filipino jobs.

86
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:28,870
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Tourism, therefore, is not merely about destinations and visitor arrivals.

87
00:13:29,190 --> 00:13:34,530
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: It is a major contributor to our economy, and more importantly, to the livelihood of our people.

88
00:13:34,950 --> 00:13:37,490
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: These figures remind us why today's economy is so important,

89
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:39,570
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and why this budget deliberation matters.

90
00:13:40,270 --> 00:13:43,850
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: We must ensure that the resources we provide to the Department

91
00:13:43,850 --> 00:13:49,610
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: are commensurate with both the opportunities and the challenges facing Philippine tourism.

92
00:13:50,310 --> 00:13:54,150
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: As a tourism advocate, this is a sector I've always felt deeply connected.

93
00:13:55,010 --> 00:13:59,670
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Coming from Sorsogon, I have seen firsthand how tourism can transform communities

94
00:13:59,670 --> 00:14:02,030
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and create opportunities for our people.

95
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:06,390
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Kasama po ako sa mga naniniwala that we should invest more in Philippine tourism.

96
00:14:06,390 --> 00:14:11,210
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: And so I look forward to a productive and constructive deliberation,

97
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:15,290
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: one where we recognize our gains, identify where we can do better,

98
00:14:15,450 --> 00:14:19,610
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: and determine how Congress and the DOT can work together to make tourism

99
00:14:19,610 --> 00:14:23,970
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: an even stronger driver of inclusive and sustainable growth.

100
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:28,570
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: With that, may I now invite Sec. Dita Angara-Mathai

101
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:31,550
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: to present the Department's proposed budget and priorities.

102
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:34,010
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Madam Secretary, you may now proceed.

103
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:36,030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Maraming salamat po.

104
00:14:36,390 --> 00:14:39,890
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Good evening, Madam Chairperson,

105
00:14:40,470 --> 00:14:42,030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Honorable Members of the Committee,

106
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,090
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and Distinguished Legislators.

107
00:14:45,070 --> 00:14:49,470
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism has been creating value for our economy and our people.

108
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:52,490
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For Fiscal Year 2027,

109
00:14:52,950 --> 00:14:57,430
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: we intend to turn this momentum into greater economic value

110
00:14:57,430 --> 00:15:00,010
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and opportunities for more Filipinos.

111
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: May I now present the Department of Tourism's performance and direction for Fiscal Year

112
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:07,820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2027.

113
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:24,430
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: First, our performance and accomplishments for 2025, second, the DOT's proposed budget

114
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:31,710
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: under the Fiscal Year 2027 National Expenditure Program, and third, the additional funding

115
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:41,030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: requirements needed to sustain our momentum and drive the next phase of tourism growth.

116
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:48,310
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our mandate is to lead the planning, development, promotion and coordination of Philippine tourism.

117
00:15:48,310 --> 00:15:51,190
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: We deliver this as one department.

118
00:15:51,190 --> 00:15:55,610
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The Central Office sets policy and strategic direction.

119
00:15:55,610 --> 00:16:01,730
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our regional offices develop destinations and tourism products, while our foreign offices

120
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:04,030
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: build markets and generate international demand.

121
00:16:04,030 --> 00:16:15,900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our agencies and corporations extend the Department's work across the tourism ecosystem, providing

122
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:24,160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: specialized support in infrastructure, heritage and destination development, dive tourism,

123
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:28,900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: retirement, visitor services and tourism promotion.

124
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:36,380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In terms of funding, our NGAs are directly funded through appropriations in the GAA,

125
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:42,880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: while our GOCCs generally operate under their corporate operating budgets.

126
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:50,980
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For Fiscal Year 2027, both Duty Free Philippines and the Tourism Promotion Board have proposed

127
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:57,940
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: budgetary support under the GAA.

128
00:16:57,940 --> 00:17:04,340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our work is delivered through four core programs, with branding as a dedicated sub-program under

129
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:07,960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: market and product development.

130
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Policy and Planning sets the direction for the development of tourism in Philippine

131
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:15,300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Industry Training develops our people.

132
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:19,560
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Standards Development and Enforcement ensures quality.

133
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:24,760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Market and Product Development turns our tourism assets into experiences that people

134
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:28,880
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: can visit, enjoy and spend on.

135
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:33,860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Branding Campaign brings these experiences to the market, strengthening the Philippine

136
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:38,460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: tourism brand and converting interest into actual travel.

137
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:47,600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: These programs connect strategy, people, quality, products and markets into one tourism development

138
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:53,010
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: system.

139
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:55,770
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The programs must translate into measurable outcomes.

140
00:17:55,770 --> 00:18:03,310
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Direct Gross Value Added measures tourism's contribution to the economy.

141
00:18:03,310 --> 00:18:09,710
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism expenditures show how visitor activity translates into spending.

142
00:18:09,710 --> 00:18:11,370
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism Employment tells us how that activity creates jobs.

143
00:18:13,370 --> 00:18:20,390
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: jobs. Tourism arrivals measure our ability to attract visitors to the Philippines. Together,

144
00:18:20,910 --> 00:18:27,990
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: these indicators tell us not only how tourism is performing, but how much value it has created

145
00:18:27,990 --> 00:18:36,320
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: for the country and for Filipinos. And the numbers show the scale of tourism's contribution to the

146
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:46,360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: economy. In 2025, tourism directly generated 2.27 trillion in economic value, equivalent to 8.1%

147
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:55,600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: of our GDP. Tourism spending was also substantial, with 3.26 trillion pesos generated by domestic

148
00:18:55,600 --> 00:19:04,160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: tourism and 698 billion pesos from international visitors. This shows that tourism is a major

149
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:06,300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: economic sector that drives tourism.

150
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:11,760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tourism spending generates jobs and supports businesses and livelihoods across the country.

151
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:20,830
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Let's look closely into the economic value of tourism, particularly to the creation of job

152
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:29,530
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: opportunities and livelihoods for millions of Filipinos. In 2025, tourism supported 7.7 million

153
00:19:29,530 --> 00:19:37,590
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: jobs, representing 15.7% of total employment in the country. That is nearly

154
00:19:37,950 --> 00:19:44,930
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: One in every six working Filipinos with tourism employment continuing to grow from 5.4 million in

155
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:55,180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2021. That economic activity is supported by continued tourism demand. From January to July

156
00:19:55,180 --> 00:20:06,220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: 2026, international visitor arrivals reached 3.93 million, up by 1.5% from 3.87 million

157
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:10,300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: during the same period last year. The United States,

158
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:18,080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: of course, remains our largest source market, followed by South Korea and Japan, while China

159
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:24,340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: has returned to make top-five markets. The challenge now is to build on these key markets

160
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:32,660
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and accelerate international tourist arrivals through the rest of the year.

161
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:39,280
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The current performance builds on the recovery achieved over the past three years. Visitor

162
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:45,200
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: arrivals increased from 5.48 million in 2023

163
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:48,600
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: to 6.48 million in 2025,

164
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: representing overall growth of 18.4 percent.

165
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:57,920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Sustaining that upward trajectory now requires us to compete more effectively for a larger

166
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:00,080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: share of the regional tourism market.

167
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:07,840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: But our performance must also be viewed with an increasingly competitive ASEAN tourism

168
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:08,280
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: market.

169
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:16,080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: In 2025, the Philippines ranked 6th in ASEAN, improving from 7th place in 2024.

170
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:24,800
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yet, with 6.48 million arrivals, we captured only 5 percent of the regional market shown

171
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:25,160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: here.

172
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:31,220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our improved ranking is encouraging, but the opportunity is much larger.

173
00:21:32,020 --> 00:21:37,080
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our task ahead is to compete for a greater share of ASEAN tourist arrivals.

174
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:39,500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Growing Tourism Market

175
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:48,360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Beyond tourist volume, our objective is to increase the economic value generated by every

176
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:48,760
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: visit.

177
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:57,480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The Philippines remained 5th in ASEAN in tourism receipts in 2025, generating about 12.15

178
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: billion U.S. dollars.

179
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:06,900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: While receipts declined slightly from 2024, our regional position was maintained despite

180
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:08,480
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: higher travel costs.

181
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:12,220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: and spending in selected categories.

182
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:19,100
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The opportunity now is to attract more visitors and generate greater value from every visit.

183
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:27,300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our regional position must also be viewed in the context of the resources behind tourism

184
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:28,300
