Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, Madam Chair and, sorry, USEC, go ahead.

1668
01:47:11,020 --> 01:47:14,800
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Madam Chair, Your Honor, may we just give figures po.

1669
01:47:14,800 --> 01:47:21,100
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: For 2026, there was an approved fund for 15 million for the Terra Madre.

1670
01:47:21,340 --> 01:47:23,500
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Under the continuing appropriations.

1671
01:47:24,040 --> 01:47:29,780
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: And then for 2027 po, we have proposed, as mentioned by Director Paolo.

1672
01:47:30,140 --> 01:47:31,680
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: But, it has not been approved.

1673
01:47:31,760 --> 01:47:34,980
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: But we can find ways, mentioned by SEC, to fund.

1674
01:47:35,140 --> 01:47:39,980
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: And we can work closely with Tourism Promotions Board on this matter din po.

1675
01:47:42,150 --> 01:47:42,590
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So,

1676
01:47:42,590 --> 01:47:51,150
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Madam Chair and Madam Secretary, I know how supportive you are and vocal about this.

1677
01:47:51,630 --> 01:47:52,470
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: We look forward.

1678
01:47:52,590 --> 01:47:54,170
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: That this may be approved.

1679
01:47:54,810 --> 01:48:00,090
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: And I do want to say, I support the Department of Tourism's budget.

1680
01:48:00,830 --> 01:48:03,590
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: At ito po, ay kailangan talagang i-priority.

1681
01:48:03,750 --> 01:48:08,190
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: Dahil tourism really brings in, again, marketing, branding, cold cash.

1682
01:48:08,570 --> 01:48:14,210
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: At ito po yung, what we are known for and what we need to invest in.

1683
01:48:14,210 --> 01:48:16,090
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, nakikita po yung returns through there.

1684
01:48:16,670 --> 01:48:21,090
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, sana po, ma-approve ito at madagdagan pa ang kanilang budget.

1685
01:48:21,290 --> 01:48:22,490
Rep. Javier Miguel Lopez Benitez: So, thank you so much.

1686
01:48:22,590 --> 01:48:25,590
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you for your support, Rep. Benitez.

1687
01:48:26,310 --> 01:48:29,510
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Next, I'll interpolate from the minority representative, Sergio Dago.

1688
01:48:31,010 --> 01:48:32,370
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1689
01:48:33,030 --> 01:48:34,490
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Magandang gabi po sa ating lahat.

1690
01:48:34,750 --> 01:48:43,030
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Lalong-lalo na kay Secretary Matay ng Tourism at sa lahat ng attached agencies.

1691
01:48:44,330 --> 01:48:52,570
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: First of all, Madam Chair, I would like to manifest my full support to the budget of the Department of Tourism.

1692
01:48:52,590 --> 01:49:02,150
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Considering that I am from Dinagat and now living in Siargao, both tourism destinations,

1693
01:49:02,770 --> 01:49:08,070
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: nakikita-kita nga kami doon ni Mark sa Siargao.

1694
01:49:08,530 --> 01:49:18,710
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Now, first of all, Madam Chair, I am alarmed with this issue paper of TIEZA.

1695
01:49:19,590 --> 01:49:21,270
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Nandito pa po yung taga-DBM?

1696
01:49:21,270 --> 01:49:21,430
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: No.

1697
01:49:22,590 --> 01:49:24,390
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala tayong from DBM?

1698
01:49:34,420 --> 01:49:44,680
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: May I ask, Madam Chair, DBM, bakit po outrightly dininayin ninyo yung request ng Tiesa for fund augmentation?

1699
01:49:45,400 --> 01:49:52,100
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Alam naman po natin na hindi po maisusulong yung mga programa ng tourism kung wala tayong infrastructure.

1700
01:49:58,800 --> 01:50:00,220
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Is there anyone from DBM?

1701
01:50:04,930 --> 01:50:08,250
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Normally naman po, pagka-budget briefing, may taga-DBM.

1702
01:50:08,250 --> 01:50:11,370
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Ma'am, you're acknowledged. Kindly state your name.

1703
01:50:11,470 --> 01:50:25,970
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Good evening, Madam Chair. Your Honor, I'm Lulu Vispo, [unclear] of the Department of Budget and Management, handling TIEZA.

1704
01:50:27,750 --> 01:50:36,030
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: May we highlight, Your Honor, that the Tiesa's proposal for national government subsidy in FY2027

1705
01:50:36,030 --> 01:50:41,050
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: is in view of several legislative measures proposing the abolition of the travel tax.

1706
01:50:41,330 --> 01:50:45,250
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: However, as these bills remain under deliberation in the Senate,

1707
01:50:46,490 --> 01:50:47,810
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: yet to be enacted into law,

1708
01:50:48,370 --> 01:50:53,470
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: the Tiesa's requested subsidy was not considered in the FY2024 NEP.

1709
01:50:54,290 --> 01:51:02,410
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: And then, however, TIEZA may continue to utilize its travel tax collections to fund tourism-related infrastructure projects,

1710
01:51:02,650 --> 01:51:07,950
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: which is consistent with Sections 72 and 73 of RA No. 9593.

1711
01:51:07,950 --> 01:51:15,110
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: So, in short po, kasi wala pa pong approval na totally abolishing yung travel tax.

1712
01:51:15,610 --> 01:51:16,210
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: So...

1713
01:51:16,490 --> 01:51:20,170
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Hindi po kami nag-recommend po.

1714
01:51:20,330 --> 01:51:26,310
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Anyway, they still have their own or corporate operating budget po for 2027.

1715
01:51:26,690 --> 01:51:37,450
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Madam Chair, may I ask the DBM, kapag ka hindi na, hindi na ipasa yung batas na yan at hindi na abolish yung tribal tax,

1716
01:51:37,830 --> 01:51:42,330
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: is there any legal impediment to augment the fund of Tiesa?

1717
01:51:46,320 --> 01:51:47,560
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Madam Chair, Your Honor,

1718
01:51:48,480 --> 01:51:52,860
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Tiesa may prioritize the utilization of its available fund,

1719
01:51:53,360 --> 01:52:03,160
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: totaling 2.355 billion, which means unobligated allotment of 810.250 as of March 31, 2026,

1720
01:52:03,160 --> 01:52:13,960
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: and 1.5 billion unreleased appropriations for FY2025 to finance the priority projects of Tiesa po.

1721
01:52:14,560 --> 01:52:18,160
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: So, meron po rin silang mga unobligated obligation.

1722
01:52:18,480 --> 01:52:21,360
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Iyon na nga po, Madam Chair.

1723
01:52:23,360 --> 01:52:30,420
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Nakikita po ba ng DBM yung pangangailangan ng infrastructure sa mga different tourist destination natin,

1724
01:52:30,520 --> 01:52:36,440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: kagaya nung halimbawa nung mga airports, although saka po yun,

1725
01:52:36,560 --> 01:52:46,460
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: pero may mga maliliit po na bagay na kinakailangan doon mga airports, mga seaports natin na pinupundungan po ng Tiesa.

1726
01:52:46,460 --> 01:52:47,640
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Hindi ko po maintindihan.

1727
01:52:47,640 --> 01:52:55,480
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Bakit napakabilis po ninyong mag-release ng tira doon sa mga, for lack of a better term,

1728
01:52:55,980 --> 01:53:02,460
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: walang mga kabuluhang project na hindi nga directly nakakatulong sa employment?

1729
01:53:03,520 --> 01:53:11,920
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pasinsya na po kasi nakikita ko po yung malaking tulong ng tourism sa mga area na nangangailangan ng employment,

1730
01:53:12,120 --> 01:53:13,000
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: pero hindi ko maintindihan.

1731
01:53:13,000 --> 01:53:17,040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, anyway, Madam Chair, maraming salamat po.

1732
01:53:17,640 --> 01:53:26,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: DBM doon sa paliwanag. Sana may parating mo kay Secretary Kim na wala naman pong legal impediment kung mag-augment tayo ng pundo.

1733
01:53:26,660 --> 01:53:33,760
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kahit kakapiranggot, may pakita lang natin na DBM is supporting our tourism industry.

1734
01:53:35,300 --> 01:53:36,220
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: Thank you, Your Honor.

1735
01:53:36,220 --> 01:53:47,240
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: But may we add also that TIEZA may also tap the SAGF of the TPB to support the development of tourism.

1736
01:53:47,640 --> 01:53:49,220
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: For enterprise zones po.

1737
01:53:49,940 --> 01:53:54,920
DBM Assistant Director Lulu P. Vispo: This is consistent with Section 55 of RA No. 9593.

1738
01:53:56,040 --> 01:54:01,140
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Sige po. Talagang binabarat nyo yung tourism.

1739
01:54:03,520 --> 01:54:09,420
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pagka pupunta po kayo ng Siargao, hindi ko kayo pasakayin ng fast craft.

1740
01:54:10,040 --> 01:54:15,040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung pinakamahina na sasakyan ng taga-DBM.

1741
01:54:15,660 --> 01:54:17,520
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: By the way,

1742
01:54:18,160 --> 01:54:25,860
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Madam Chair, may I ask D.O.T., mayroon po ba kayong malalim na ugnayan sa D.N.R.?

1743
01:54:25,860 --> 01:54:35,040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung regular na ugnayan sa D.N.R.?

1744
01:54:35,040 --> 01:54:49,180
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: I'm asking that, Madam Chair, kasi I think the good Secretary will agree with me na hindi po pwedeng magkatabi yung mining at saka tourism.

1745
01:54:49,420 --> 01:54:50,600
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: That's the point I am raising.

1746
01:54:53,680 --> 01:54:56,080
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Usec Majo, you are recognized.

1747
01:54:56,400 --> 01:55:09,690
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Madam Chair, Your Honor, we have convergence program with them, with the D.N.R.

1748
01:55:09,810 --> 01:55:19,710
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So we have what we call the Sustainable Tourism Program, which aim to protect and ensure the sustainability of Philippine tourism resources and attractions.

1749
01:55:19,930 --> 01:55:27,090
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So we have partners under this program, D.N.R., the WWF Philippines and the NCCA.

1750
01:55:27,270 --> 01:55:29,530
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: And we have training areas.

1751
01:55:29,990 --> 01:55:36,750
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Regularly, sustainable tourism, sustainable dining, and community eco-guiding.

1752
01:55:36,750 --> 01:55:39,570
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So meron po kaming tulungan doon.

1753
01:55:39,630 --> 01:55:46,990
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: And we have conducted 13 trainings and 417 participants trained na po.

1754
01:55:47,210 --> 01:55:52,250
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: That's the collaboration we have under the convergence program, Your Honor, Madam Chair.

1755
01:55:52,610 --> 01:55:55,950
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Madam Chair, maganda pong pakinggan yung programa na yon.

1756
01:55:56,770 --> 01:55:59,950
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pero ang tinutukoy ko po dito, paano nyo in-implement yan?

1757
01:55:59,990 --> 01:56:06,870
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Alam nyo ba yung dinagat? Nakikita ba ng taga-regional office yung mukha ng mga kabundukan ng dinagat?

1758
01:56:06,990 --> 01:56:08,950
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: But we are promoting tourism there.

1759
01:56:12,560 --> 01:56:17,100
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Alam nyo yung bonsai forest sa Loreto? That's a tourism destination?

1760
01:56:17,740 --> 01:56:25,660
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Tapos bakit kung mayroon kayong malalim na ugnayan ng DENR, bakit hindi nyo nakita na naisyuhan ng mga MPSA yan?

1761
01:56:26,300 --> 01:56:29,060
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Why did the Department of Tourism allow that?

1762
01:56:36,570 --> 01:56:38,870
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Sec. Dita, you're recognized

1763
01:56:38,870 --> 01:56:39,450
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Bukas po.

1764
01:56:39,810 --> 01:56:52,790
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: I'm going to speak in a heritage event. Ang kasama ko po si DENR [unclear]. Kakausapin ko po siya nang masinsinan po.

1765
01:56:53,410 --> 01:56:58,790
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: At sasabihin ko, kung hindi siya, hindi niya ako papansin, susumuko siya sa inyo.

1766
01:57:00,550 --> 01:57:04,710
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Madam Chair, ako, I am a living witness, how tourism, no?

1767
01:57:06,910 --> 01:57:09,690
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Help, no? Our employment.

1768
01:57:09,810 --> 01:57:12,030
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Unemployment problem. Unemployment problem.

1769
01:57:13,270 --> 01:57:21,930
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: What I am recommending, Madam Chair, is that sana, you could have an inventory sa mga tourism destinations natin.

1770
01:57:22,550 --> 01:57:24,470
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Talk with D.N.R., coordinate with D.N.R.

1771
01:57:24,790 --> 01:57:27,810
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Dapat itong mga area na to, wag kayong isyo ng isyo ng...

1772
01:57:28,730 --> 01:57:34,810
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Lahat, pagka sumakay ka ng aeroplano papuntang Siargao, nakikita mo pagdaan mo sa dinagat.

1773
01:57:36,090 --> 01:57:38,450
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala na po yung baybayin ng dinagat.

1774
01:57:38,570 --> 01:57:39,810
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Parehas lang po ng Siargao.

1775
01:57:39,810 --> 01:57:43,350
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Siargao ang klase, pero ano na po siya.

1776
01:57:45,190 --> 01:57:48,770
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Tingnan nyo na lang, yung sa regional office, tingnan nyo doon.

1777
01:57:49,390 --> 01:57:49,750
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Opo.

1778
01:57:51,070 --> 01:57:59,690
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Can I get a commitment from the good secretary na laliman nyo yung ugnayan nyo with D.N.R.

1779
01:58:00,930 --> 01:58:07,670
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: In particular, yung dinagat, which is, has a big potential, no?

1780
01:58:07,670 --> 01:58:08,670
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: As a next...

1781
01:58:09,810 --> 01:58:13,650
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Tourism destination doon sa Caraga.

1782
01:58:14,450 --> 01:58:17,230
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yes, sir. You have our commitment. Thank you very much, po.

1783
01:58:18,350 --> 01:58:22,990
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala na kong time, Madam Chair, sa plenary na lang.

1784
01:58:23,590 --> 01:58:34,150
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pero, in the proper time, I will support, no, Madam Chair, in the proper time, the augmentation of the budget of the DOT.

1785
01:58:34,810 --> 01:58:36,670
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Most particularly, the TIEZA.

1786
01:58:38,350 --> 01:58:39,290
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you.

1787
01:58:39,290 --> 01:58:39,350
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you.

1788
01:58:39,350 --> 01:58:39,650
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you.

1789
01:58:39,650 --> 01:58:39,790
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you.

1790
01:58:39,790 --> 01:58:40,970
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Thank you, Representative Dagooc.

1791
01:58:41,170 --> 01:58:47,170
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Before we proceed, I would like to acknowledge the presence of Deputy Majority Leader Howard Guintu.

1792
01:58:48,230 --> 01:58:52,630
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Next, to interpellate, from the majority, Representative Salvador Pleyto.

1793
01:58:53,450 --> 01:58:54,850
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1794
01:58:55,710 --> 01:58:57,470
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Magandang gabi po sa ating lahat.

1795
01:58:57,930 --> 01:59:02,890
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Kay Secretary Matay, saka DOT family.

1796
01:59:03,290 --> 01:59:13,690
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Madam Chair, it is being said that tourism cannot thrive.

1797
01:59:13,690 --> 01:59:16,330
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: thrive on beautiful destinations alone.

1798
01:59:17,470 --> 01:59:21,130
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Natural appeal and rich culture are only half the equation.

1799
01:59:22,610 --> 01:59:26,110
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Sustainable growth requires supporting physical infrastructure.

1800
01:59:27,010 --> 01:59:36,870
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Kailangan po ng dependable roads, airports, ports, reliable water supply, proper sanitation, telecommunications, and stable electricity.

1801
01:59:37,150 --> 01:59:42,190
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: While the Department of Tourism leads marketing and destination development,

1802
01:59:42,190 --> 01:59:46,250
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: its success hinges on interagency alignment.

1803
01:59:47,150 --> 01:59:52,290
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Without synchronized investment across basic services,

1804
01:59:52,930 --> 01:59:58,130
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: high potential sites across our regions will remain underutilized.

1805
01:59:58,130 --> 01:59:59,690
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: underperforming,

1806
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:04,540
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: or inaccessible to both local and international tourists.

1807
02:00:05,560 --> 02:00:08,380
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: In view of that, I would like to seek clarification, Secretary,

1808
02:00:08,900 --> 02:00:12,380
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: from the Department on the following operational points.

1809
02:00:13,060 --> 02:00:16,340
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: May I ask Undersecretary Guillermo,

1810
02:00:17,020 --> 02:00:20,340
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: kasi narinig ko kanina na sumasagot tungkol dito sa aking tanong,

1811
02:00:22,570 --> 02:00:28,230
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: what specific tourism sites have been identified by the Department of Tourism

1812
02:00:28,230 --> 02:00:35,530
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: as high potential but whose visitor growth remains affected by inadequate infrastructure?

1813
02:00:36,290 --> 02:00:37,090
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1814
02:00:37,990 --> 02:00:39,710
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Usec Majo, you're recognized.

1815
02:00:45,880 --> 02:00:47,680
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Thank you, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

1816
02:00:47,680 --> 02:00:50,740
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So, we have, as we have mentioned before,

1817
02:00:51,360 --> 02:00:54,760
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: we were looking into focusing,

1818
02:00:55,280 --> 02:00:58,480
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: well, the OT strategic direction is focused really on connectivity,

1819
02:00:59,100 --> 02:01:03,360
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: domestic tourism, destination readiness, investment, and ease of entry.

1820
02:01:03,740 --> 02:01:09,840
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: Our key transport projects include the new Manila International Airport in Bulacan

1821
02:01:09,840 --> 02:01:13,860
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: and the proposed railway connectivity between Bulacan and Clark.

1822
02:01:14,040 --> 02:01:18,000
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So, we do acknowledge that it cannot solve infrastructure gaps alone.

1823
02:01:18,380 --> 02:01:21,760
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So, different agencies have also distinct roles to address the gaps.

1824
02:01:22,220 --> 02:01:27,860
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: So, we have DPWH, we have convergence with them for the implementation of road construction

1825
02:01:27,860 --> 02:01:33,160
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: and then we also have the DOTr that implements airports,

1826
02:01:33,380 --> 02:01:35,740
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: ports and transport infrastructure development.

1827
02:01:36,560 --> 02:01:44,040
DOT Undersecretary Ma. Dionesa A. Rivera-Guillermo: We also have the PIDS, the Philippine Institute for Development Studies,

